</div>
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Apical (Periapical) Abscess</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Bacteria reach the tooth root tip through untreated decay, causing a pus-filled pocket at the root apex that erodes surrounding bone.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Facial Space Infection</h1><p class="text-on-surface-variant">From a lower back tooth, infection spreads into the submasseteric or submandibular space. From an upper tooth, it can spread toward the eye (orbital cellulitis).</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Ludwig's Angina</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A life-threatening floor-of-mouth infection that rapidly spreads bilaterally. Causes airway obstruction and requires immediate hospital admission.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Cavernous Sinus Thrombosis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Infection spreading via facial veins to the cavernous sinus behind the eyes — causes double vision, eye protrusion, and can be fatal.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Jaw Bone Infection</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Chronic untreated tooth infection spreads into the jawbone (osteomyelitis), requiring prolonged IV antibiotics and possible surgical debridement.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Systemic (Sepsis)</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Bacteria entering the bloodstream from a dental infection can cause sepsis — a全身-wide inflammatory response that is a medical emergency.</p></div>
</div>
