<h3 class="font-headline-sm text-primary">Surgical Treatment</h3>
</div>
<ul class="space-y-6">
<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Tooth Extraction</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Non-restorable teeth and those with severe bone loss require extraction — eliminates the source of infection immediately.</p></li>
<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Incision and Drainage</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">For fluctuating facial swellings, surgical drainage provides immediate pain relief and allows direct antibiotic delivery into the infected space.</p></li>
<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Debridement / Resection</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Jawbone (osteomyelitis) or extensive tissue involvement requires surgical debridement of dead and infected tissue alongside prolonged antibiotics.</p></li>
</ul>
